# Form field settings (golden rule)

Every **datagrid / datatable** that has a **+ New row** (create/edit modal) must also expose a **Settings** nav tab beside the feature in the module header.

## Header navigation

- Do **not** add Settings to the module header nav links.
- Settings is accessed from the grid toolbar only (see below).

## Grid toolbar

- Pass `settingsHref` to `SpreadsheetGrid` beside **+ New row**.
- Render as a **cog icon** button (built into `SpreadsheetGrid`); link to the feature settings route (e.g. `/app/inventory/partners/settings`).
- Register settings routes in `web/src/App.tsx`; hrefs live in `web/src/shared/entityTypes.ts` (`INVENTORY_SETTINGS_HREF`) or equivalent per module.

## Settings page

Use `EntityFormSettingsPage` from `web/src/shared/EntityFormSettingsPage.tsx` (or a thin wrapper per feature).

Admins can configure **all form fields** for the new-row modal:

| Field kind | Configurable |
|------------|--------------|
| Standard (built-in) | Label override, visible, required, disabled |
| Custom (tenant-defined) | Label, visible, required, active; add new; remove (soft-delete) |

## API

- `GET/PATCH /api/v1/form-field-settings?entity_type=…` — merged standard + custom settings (`api/internal/platform/formfields`).
- `POST/DELETE /api/v1/custom-fields` — create / deactivate custom field definitions.
- Standard field registry per entity lives in `api/internal/platform/formfields/registry.go`.
- DB: `tenant_standard_field_settings` (migration `005_form_field_settings.sql`).

## Create/edit modal

1. Wrap standard fields with `ModalField` + `useFormFieldSettings` so visibility, labels, required, and disabled state come from settings.
2. Render custom values with `CustomFieldsSection` (read-only config; no inline field builder).
3. Validate with `buildRequiredChecks` + `validateCustomFields` before save.

## New features checklist

When adding a new grid with new-row modals:

1. Add entity type to `formfields/registry.go` and `web/src/shared/entityTypes.ts` (include `INVENTORY_SETTINGS_HREF` entry).
2. Add feature in `modules.ts` and routes in `App.tsx` (grid + settings page).
3. Create `*SettingsPage.tsx` wrapper using `EntityFormSettingsPage`.
4. Pass `settingsHref` to `SpreadsheetGrid`; use `ModalField` / `CustomFieldsSection` in the modal.
5. Run migration if new standard-field table changes are needed.

See also: `.cursor/rules/custom-form-fields.mdc` for custom field types and admin roles.
